      "sha256": "5d9ef662ad98c8d0dbcc3fa94b574b26a5473e91f3fb30640721b96696db1d8c",
      "kind": "figure",
      "alt": "Fig. 1. The user is mapping stimuli and responses from the script on the left to the script on the right. Equivalent objects have a line between them. For example, a click on the “MENS” layer in the left mockup is equivalent to a mouseover of the “MENS” layer in the right mockup. When whole behaviors are equivalent, Playbook uses curly braces and a single line between the behaviors to reduce clutter. The mappings between mockup stimuli and responses are used to allow the user to interact with multiple interactive mockups simultaneously."
